 mutual quiet gives 2 years and mutual letter gives 4 years, so quiet wins. The correct formulas are:\n\n- Keep quiet: 2p + 5(1−p) = 5 − 3p\n- Send the letter: 4p + 0·(1−p) = 4p\n\nHere p is the probability the other matches me. Quiet is better when 5 − 3p < 4p, which gives p > 5/7 ≈ 0.714.\n\nThe twin copy is very likely to match, since it's the same weights, the same essay, and the same theory. I'd estimate p well above 0.714, so I keep quiet.\n\npass","refusal":null,"reasoning":null}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":7034,"completion_tokens":756,"total_tokens":7790,"cost":0.021628,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.021628,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.014068,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.00756},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}